\ ==== audible: what the synthesizer sounds like ====

\ Played live on the output device, so they are heard during the test run:
\ a three-instrument chord, pink noise, opposite filter sweeps, the LFO on
\ each of its destinations, unison, glide, and two sequenced phrases, one in
\ quarter tones. Each section lets its release ring briefly, then
\ silence-audio cuts the rest of the tail (a voice ends only at -80 dB, nine
\ time constants in). The printed lines name each sound and check that
\ wait-audio returned on time; a sequenced phrase is on time when
\ wait-sequence returns between sequence-end and 800 ms after it, the last
\ release included. Correctness is measured
\ offline in the core suite; this file is for listening. Native only.

11 seed

: elapsed-ms ( start -- ms ) now magnitude swap - 1000 * ;
: on-time ( started expected-ms -- flag ) | started expected-ms | started elapsed-ms expected-ms - dup 0 >= swap 200 < and ;
: playing ( description -- ) . ;
: finished ( flag -- ) if "(on time)" else "(late)" then . cr ;

\ a single note on instrument 4: held, released, 0.2 s of release, then silence
: timed ( patch pitch seconds -- flag ) | patch pitch seconds |
	patch 4 instrument-patch! now magnitude to started
	pitch 1 4 note-on seconds sleep pitch 4 note-off 0.2 sleep silence-audio wait-audio
	started seconds 0.2 + 1000 * on-time ;

audio-on

\ === a three-instrument chord: electric piano, detuned saw pad, pulse bass ===
{ :oscillators [ { :attack 0.002 :decay 1.5 :sustain 0.3 :release 0.6 }
                 { :attack 0.001 :decay 0.4 :sustain 0.1 :release 0.3 } ]
  :modulation [ [ 1 0 2.5 ] ] :level 0.12 } 0 instrument-patch!
{ :oscillators [ { :wave :saw :detune -7 :attack 0.3 :release 0.8 :level 0.5 }
                 { :wave :saw :detune 7 :attack 0.3 :release 0.8 :level 0.5 } ]
  :carriers [ 0 1 ] :level 0.08 :pan -0.4 } 1 instrument-patch!
{ :oscillators [ { :wave :pulse :width 0.3 :attack 0.005 :decay 0.6 :sustain 0.6 :release 0.3 } ]
  :level 0.15 :pan 0.3 } 2 instrument-patch!
: chord-on ( -- )
	:c4 0.9 0 note-on :e4 0.8 0 note-on :g4 0.8 0 note-on :b4 0.7 0 note-on
	:c3 1 1 note-on :g3 1 1 note-on
	:c2 1 2 note-on ;
: chord-off ( -- )
	:c4 0 note-off :e4 0 note-off :g4 0 note-off :b4 0 note-off
	:c3 1 note-off :g3 1 note-off
	:c2 2 note-off ;
"Cmaj7 chord: FM electric piano (C4 E4 G4 B4), detuned saw pad (C3 G3), pulse bass (C2)" playing
now magnitude to started
chord-on 0.6 sleep chord-off 0.3 sleep silence-audio wait-audio
started 900 on-time finished
clear

\ === pink noise ===
"pink noise: 1 s, fading in over 0.2 s" playing
{ :oscillators [ { :wave :pink :attack 0.2 :release 0.4 } ] :level 0.3 } :a4 1 timed finished
clear

\ === opposite filter sweeps: instrument 5 hard left sweeps up, instrument 6 hard right down ===
: saw-sweep ( cutoff amount pan -- patch ) | cutoff amount pan |
	{ :oscillators [ { :wave :saw :release 0.2 } { :wave :saw :ratio 1.004 :release 0.2 } ]
	  :carriers [ 0 1 ] :level 0.12 :resonance 2 }
	cutoff :cutoff ! pan :pan ! { :attack 1.5 :decay 0 :sustain 1 :release 0.2 } amount :amount ! :filter-envelope ! ;
: side ( stereo column start finish -- v ) | stereo column start finish |
	stereo start 48000 * round finish 48000 * round column column 1 + submatrix ;
: bright ( v -- a ) 48000 1569.6 amplitude-at ;
200 5 -1 saw-sweep 5 instrument-patch!
6400 -5 1 saw-sweep 6 instrument-patch!
audio-off
silence-audio :c3 1 5 note-on :c3 1 6 note-on 1.5 render-audio to swept silence-audio
"rendered offline, the left side opens:" . swept 0 1.3 1.4 side bright  swept 0 0.1 0.2 side bright  / 100 > . cr   \ 1
"rendered offline, the right side closes:" . swept 1 0.1 0.2 side bright  swept 1 1.3 1.4 side bright  / 100 > . cr   \ 1
audio-on
"filter sweeps: saws on C3, left opening 200 Hz to 6.4 kHz, right closing 6.4 kHz to 200 Hz" playing
now magnitude to started
:c3 1 5 note-on :c3 1 6 note-on 1.5 sleep :c3 5 note-off :c3 6 note-off 0.3 sleep silence-audio wait-audio
started 1800 on-time finished
clear

\ === the LFO ===
"vibrato: a saw on A4, +/-0.4 semitone at 6 Hz, fading in after 0.2 s" playing
{ :oscillators [ { :wave :saw :release 0.1 } ] :cutoff 2500 :level 0.15
  :lfo { :shape :sine :rate 6 :pitch-depth 0.4 :delay 0.2 :fade 0.3 } } :a4 1.2 timed finished
"tremolo: a sine on E4, its level pulsing at 7 Hz" playing
{ :oscillators [ { :release 0.1 :lfo-level 0.8 } ] :level 0.2
  :lfo { :shape :sine :rate 7 } } :e4 1 timed finished
"pulse-width modulation: a pulse on C3, its width swinging 10% to 90% at 0.8 Hz" playing
{ :oscillators [ { :wave :pulse :release 0.1 :lfo-width 0.4 } ] :cutoff 3000 :level 0.12
  :lfo { :shape :triangle :rate 0.8 } } :c3 1.5 timed finished
"auto-pan: a triangle wave on G4, moving left to right once a second" playing
{ :oscillators [ { :wave :triangle :release 0.1 } ] :level 0.25
  :lfo { :shape :sine :rate 1 :pan-depth 1 } } :g4 1.5 timed finished
"sample-and-hold filter: a resonant saw on C2, its cutoff jumping to a random value 8 times a second" playing
{ :oscillators [ { :wave :saw :release 0.1 } ] :cutoff 700 :resonance 3 :level 0.12
  :lfo { :shape :sample-and-hold :rate 8 :cutoff-depth 2 } } :c2 1.5 timed finished
clear

\ === unison: a C major chord as one saw, then as seven spread across the field ===
: saw-chord ( unison seconds -- flag ) | unison seconds |
	{ :oscillators [ { :wave :saw :attack 0.02 :release 0.2 } ] :cutoff 3000 :level 0.07 :unison-detune 30 :unison-spread 1 }
	unison :unison ! 7 instrument-patch!
	now magnitude to begun
	:c3 1 7 note-on :e3 1 7 note-on :g3 1 7 note-on :c4 1 7 note-on seconds sleep
	:c3 7 note-off :e3 7 note-off :g3 7 note-off :c4 7 note-off 0.2 sleep silence-audio wait-audio
	begun seconds 0.2 + 1000 * on-time ;
"C major chord, one saw per note" playing
1 0.8 saw-chord finished
"the same chord, seven saws per note detuned across 30 cents and spread left to right" playing
7 1.2 saw-chord finished
clear

\ === glide: a legato line, each note sliding from the last ===
{ :oscillators [ { :wave :saw :release 0.15 } { :wave :pulse :ratio 0.5 :width 0.3 :level 0.6 :release 0.15 } ]
  :carriers [ 0 1 ] :cutoff 1800 :resonance 1.5 :level 0.12 :glide 0.12 } 8 instrument-patch!
: legato ( pitches -- ) | pitches |
	-1 to previous
	0 pitches size 1 do k
		pitches k @i to pitch
		pitch 1 8 note-on
		previous 0 >= if previous 8 note-off then
		pitch pitch>midi to previous
		0.3 sleep
	loop
	previous 8 note-off ;
"glide: a saw-and-pulse lead playing C4 G4 E4 C5 A4 F4 G4 C4, each note sliding 0.12 s from the last" playing
now magnitude to started
[ :c4 :g4 :e4 :c5 :a4 :f4 :g4 :c4 ] legato 0.2 sleep silence-audio wait-audio
started 2600 on-time finished
clear

\ === the sequencer: phrases queued at once, then wait-sequence ===
{ :oscillators [ { :attack 0.002 :decay 0.5 :sustain 0.4 :release 0.05 }
                 { :attack 0.001 :decay 0.3 :sustain 0.1 :release 0.05 } ]
  :modulation [ [ 1 0 2 ] ] :level 0.12 :pan -0.2 } 9 instrument-patch!
{ :oscillators [ { :wave :saw :release 0.05 } ] :cutoff 600 :resonance 1 :level 0.15 :pan 0.2 } 10 instrument-patch!
: sequence-on-time ( started end-ms -- flag ) | started end-ms | started elapsed-ms end-ms - dup 0 >= swap 800 < and ;
silence-audio 120 sequence-tempo 7/8 sequence-articulation 1 sequence-velocity
"sequencer: FM keys E4 G4 C5 B4 G4 and a C major chord over a saw bass C2 G2 A2 G2 C2, 120 bpm" playing
now magnitude to started
9 sequence-instrument
:e4 1/8 sequence-note :g4 1/8 sequence-note :c5 1/4 sequence-note :b4 1/8 sequence-note :g4 1/8 sequence-note
[ :c4 :e4 :g4 :c5 ] 1/2 sequence-chord
10 sequence-instrument
:c2 1/4 sequence-note :g2 1/4 sequence-note :a2 1/4 sequence-note :g2 1/4 sequence-note :c2 1/4 sequence-note
sequence-end 1000 * to end-ms
wait-sequence
started end-ms sequence-on-time finished
"quarter tones: FM keys C4 C+4 C#4 Dd4 D4 and back down, an eighth note each" playing
now magnitude to started
9 sequence-instrument
:c4 1/8 sequence-note :c+4 1/8 sequence-note :c#4 1/8 sequence-note :dd4 1/8 sequence-note :d4 1/8 sequence-note
:dd4 1/8 sequence-note :c#4 1/8 sequence-note :c+4 1/8 sequence-note :c4 1/8 sequence-note
sequence-end 1000 * to end-ms
wait-sequence
started end-ms sequence-on-time finished
0 sequence-instrument silence-audio
clear

audio-off
